    `the examination is by the adverse party` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the examination is of a witness who was cross-examined and is then examined by the party who called the witness` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the examination relates to relevant facts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the re-examination is directed to the explanation of matters referred to in cross-examination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `new matter is introduced in re-examination by permission of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- sections 143 to 145
    `the question suggests the answer which the person putting it wishes or expects to receive, or suggests disputed facts as to which the witness is to testify` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the adverse party objects to the leading question` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court permits the leading question` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the question is as to a matter which is introductory or undisputed, or which has in the court's opinion already been sufficiently proved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the question puts into the mouth of the witness the very words which the witness is to echo back` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the question assumes that facts have been proved which have not been proved, or that particular answers have been given contrary to the fact` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court has prohibited leading questions to a witness who shows a strong interest or bias in favour of the cross-examining party` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 146 and Explanation"
DECLARE `Matters in Writing Facts` HAS
    `the witness says that a contract, grant or other disposition of property as to which the witness is giving evidence was contained in a document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the witness is about to make a statement as to the contents of a document which in the opinion of the court ought to be produced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the evidence is of statements made by other persons about the contents of documents, and the statements are in themselves relevant facts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the document has been produced, or facts have been proved which entitle the party who called the witness to give secondary evidence of it` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, ss 147, 159"
DECLARE `Previous Statement Facts` HAS
    -- section 147(1) and (2)
    `the previous statement was made in writing or reduced into writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the previous statement was oral` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the previous statement is relevant to matters in question in the proceeding in which the witness is cross-examined` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the previous statement is inconsistent with the witness's present testimony` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the witness does not distinctly admit that the witness made the oral statement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is intended to contradict the witness by the writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the witness's attention was called, before the writing is proved, to the parts of it which are to be used for contradicting the witness` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the circumstances of the supposed oral statement, sufficient to designate the particular occasion, were mentioned to the witness and the witness was asked whether the witness made it` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- section 147(3)
    `the previous inconsistent or contradictory statement is proved by virtue of section 147` IS A BOOLEAN
    `direct oral evidence of the fact stated by the maker would be admissible` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- section 147(4) and (5)
    `the witness is cross-examined on a document used by the witness to refresh the witness's memory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the document is received in evidence by virtue of section 147(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- section 147(7)
    `a written law or rule of practice requires the evidence given by the maker of the statement to be corroborated or regulates the manner in which it is treated if uncorroborated` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- section 159
    `the witness whom it is intended to corroborate has given testimony` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the former statement relates to the same fact` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the former statement was made at or about the time when the fact took place, or before an authority legally competent to investigate the fact` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, ss 148 to 155"
DECLARE `Credibility Question Facts` HAS
    `the witness may be cross-examined` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the question tends to test the witness's accuracy, veracity or credibility` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the question tends to discover who the witness is and what the witness's position in life is` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the question tends to shake the witness's credit by injuring the witness's character` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the question relates to a matter relevant to the suit or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the imputation conveyed is such that its truth would seriously affect the court's opinion as to the witness's credibility on the matter to which the witness testifies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the imputation relates to matters so remote in time or of such character that its truth would not affect, or would affect only slightly, the court's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a great disproportion between the importance of the imputation and the importance of the witness's evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person asking the question has reasonable grounds for thinking that the imputation is well founded` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the question is indecent or scandalous` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the question relates to a fact in issue or to a matter necessary to be known in order to determine whether the facts in issue existed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the question appears to the court to be intended to insult or annoy, or appears needlessly offensive in form although proper in itself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused is charged with committing a sexual offence or child abuse offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the witness has been asked and has answered a question relevant only insofar as it tends to shake the witness's credit by injuring character` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the question was whether the witness has been previously convicted of a crime and the witness denies it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the question tended to impeach the witness's impartiality and the witness answered by denying the facts suggested` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, ss 157, 158, 160, 160A"
DECLARE `Impeachment and Corroboration Facts` HAS
    `the credit of the witness is impeached by the adverse party` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the credit of the witness is impeached by the party who calls the witness with the consent of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the evidence is of persons who testify that from their knowledge of the witness they believe the witness unworthy of credit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the evidence is proof that the witness has been bribed, has accepted the offer of a bribe, or has received another corrupt inducement to give evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the evidence is proof of former statements inconsistent with a part of the witness's evidence which is liable to be contradicted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the witness gives evidence of a relevant fact and is questioned as to other circumstances observed at or near the time or place of that fact` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is of the opinion that those circumstances, if proved, would corroborate the testimony of the witness as to the relevant fact` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proceedings are criminal proceedings and the corroborating evidence is the evidence of another witness` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a statement relevant under section 32 or 33 has been proved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement is admissible by virtue of section 32(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement is admissible by virtue of section 32(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the evidence to be corroborated was given by the maker of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the evidence to be corroborated was given by the person who originally supplied the information from which the statement was made` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, ss 161 to 166"
DECLARE `Refreshing Memory Facts` HAS
    `the writing was made by the witness at the time of the transaction, or so soon afterwards that the court considers it likely that the transaction was then fresh in the witness's memory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the writing was made by another person and was read by the witness within that time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the witness knew it to be correct when the witness read it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the witness refers to a copy of the document with the permission of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is satisfied that there is sufficient reason for the non-production of the original` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the witness is an expert referring to a professional treatise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the witness has no specific recollection of the facts but is sure that the facts were correctly recorded in the document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the adverse party requires the writing to be produced and shown` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the party called for a document that the party gave the other party notice to produce, and it was produced and inspected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the party producing it requires the party who called for it to give it as evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the document is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the party refused to produce a document that the party had notice to produce` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other party consents or the court orders that the document be used` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, ss 164, 167, 169"
DECLARE `Court Power Facts` HAS
    `the witness was summoned to produce a document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the document is in the witness's possession or power` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the document refers to affairs of State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the witness would be entitled under sections 123 to 133 to refuse to answer the question or produce the document if the adverse party asked or called for it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the question would be improper for any other person to ask under section 150 or 151` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Judge proposes to dispense with the primary evidence of a document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the case is one excepted in the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there was sufficient evidence to justify the decision independently of the evidence objected to and admitted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rejected evidence, if received, ought not to have varied the decision` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Part 4 -- Bankers' books: sections 170 to 176`

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, ss 170 to 175"
DECLARE `Bankers Books Facts` HAS
    `the book was, at the time of the making of the entry, one of the ordinary books of the bank` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entry was made in the usual and ordinary course of business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the book is in the custody or control of the bank` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the copy has been examined with the original entry and is correct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the bank is a party to the legal proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a judge has ordered the production or attendance for special cause` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the company carries on the business of bankers in Singapore under a licence granted under a law relating to banking` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Part 5 and the Schedules`

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, First Schedule, Part 1"
DECLARE `Kind of Offence Class` IS ONE OF
    `a child abuse offence`
    `a sexual offence`
    `neither`

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, First Schedule and s 3(1) 'child abuse offence', 'sexual offence'"
DECLARE `Scheduled Offence Facts` HAS
    `the Act under which the offence is created` IS A STRING
    `the section number` IS A STRING
    `the offence is an attempt to commit, an abetment of, or being a party to a criminal conspiracy to commit, an offence in the Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, Second Schedule"
DECLARE `Statutory Body Row` HAS
    `statutory body` IS A STRING
    `Act under which established` IS A STRING

§ `The facts about one item of evidence, bundled`

-- The Criminal Procedure Code's questions about a statement are answered from several of the records above
-- (section 147, 157, 32, 33, 17 to 23, 47, 122(4)); this record carries them together so that one question can be asked of one
-- item of evidence.  It adds no fact of its own.
@ref "Evidence Act 1893, ss 17 to 23, 32, 33, 47, 122(4), 147, 157, 159; Criminal Procedure Code 2010, ss 259, 268, 269, 291"
DECLARE `Evidence Act Fact Bundle` HAS
    `previous statement facts` IS A `Previous Statement Facts`
    `impeachment and corroboration facts` IS AN `Impeachment and Corroboration Facts`
    `hearsay facts` IS A `Hearsay Facts`
    `former testimony facts` IS A `Former Testimony Facts`
    `admission facts` IS AN `Admission Facts`
    `opinion facts` IS AN `Opinion Facts`
    `accused cross-examination facts` IS AN `Accused Cross-examination Facts`
